From 122d734b69cedef271dcf06ea5d3f2d17f8de8d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex <6164003+alex-kish@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:10:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] egl: map the display in eglGetConfigAttrib

eglGetConfigAttrib was turned from a HYBRIS_EGL_IMPLEMENT_FUNCTION4 wrapper
into a hand-written function (to call ws_getConfigAttrib) in 38de2ac, but
the new function passes the hybris display handle straight to the Android
EGL. On the wayland window system that handle is a struct _EGLDisplay *,
so every call fails with EGL_BAD_DISPLAY. Clients that check config
attributes (RetroArch, SDL, ...) then find no usable EGL config.

Pass hybris_egl_get_real_display(dpy), like the other wrappers do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 hybris/egl/egl.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hybris/egl/egl.c b/hybris/egl/egl.c
index 8bbd4d1..321b732 100644
--- a/hybris/egl/egl.c
+++ b/hybris/egl/egl.c
@@ -638,7 +638,7 @@ EGLBoolean eglGetConfigAttrib(EGLDisplay dpy, EGLConfig config, EGLint attribute
 	EGLBoolean ret;
 	HYBRIS_TRACE_BEGIN("hybris-egl", "eglGetConfigAttrib", "");
 	HYBRIS_DLSYSM(egl, &_eglGetConfigAttrib, "eglGetConfigAttrib");
-	ret = (*_eglGetConfigAttrib)(dpy, config, attribute, value);
+	ret = (*_eglGetConfigAttrib)(hybris_egl_get_real_display(dpy), config, attribute, value);
 	ws_getConfigAttrib(&dpy, &config, &attribute, value);
 	HYBRIS_TRACE_END("hybris-egl", "eglGetConfigAttrib", "");
 	return ret;
